From c86e462173de5542f9e7adc0322c81a5178d4675 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:53:53 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mask): pad off-frame crops so lips at the frame edge are
 still detected

When the face leaves through a frame edge, the lip check clipped its square crop to the
frame and stretched the remainder to 512x512; the distorted half-face hid the lips from the
parser and lips beside the wearable stayed exposed (seen at 14.3 s of the test clip).
Off-frame parts are now padded with neutral grey, for both the lip check and the
mouth-visibility check of untracked frames.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015XEHdEnhr7p5ae4FL4TjbE
---
 app/processing.py        | 20 ++++++++++++++++----
 tests/test_lip_safety.py | 24 +++++++++++++++++++-----
 2 files changed, 35 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/processing.py b/app/processing.py
index 8d17b3e..bff9aba 100644
--- a/app/processing.py
+++ b/app/processing.py
